From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:07:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11340/11362] fix(arc): grammar requires source definitions;
 force turn is submission-only

Review closures for REQ-ARC-WMTE-7046, plus the record of the bounded 27B
trial and its harness.

What the review found (confirmed against test-gbnf-validator, b9606):
1. `list_transitions` has no required parameter, so its `{}` call stayed
   the cheapest legal envelope. In the 27B trial every grammar cell chose
   it first and submitted code only after the force nudge. So the nudge,
   not the grammar, was doing the enforcement.
2. `nonempty-string` admitted `{"code":" "}`, which passed the lifter,
   dispatched, and counted as a parsed call.
3. The spec cited an untracked, incomplete note.

What changed:
- `REQUIRED_SOURCE_DEFINITIONS` (arc_induction_tools.py): a source argument
  must contain the definition dispatch looks for: `def engine(`,
  `def is_level_complete(`, `def accept(`. The grammar rule is
  `"\"" char* "def engine(" char* "\"" ws`. The threshold is the
  dispatcher's own contract, not a character count. `{"code":"def engine("}`
  is the admitted minimum and fails at dispatch as a syntax error; the
  verifier judges programs, the grammar cannot.
- `_lift_grammar_response` rejects a blank required string and a source
  argument without its definition. No dispatch, not counted as parsed.
- `_tool_grammar(schemas, allowed=...)`: at the loop's force turn the
  request carries a grammar whose root admits only
  `run_engine_on_transitions`. The nudge text stays. Counted in
  `grammar_submit_only_turns`.
- 52 of 52 verdicts re-established against the binary (26 strings x 2
  grammars: full sha256 16578b60ac14f9f2, submission-only c83115a92f437134);
  the Python reader agreed on all 52. Pinned in test_gbnf_match.py.
- Mutations M5-M8 at the call sites: RED, byte-identical restore, GREEN.
  205 focused tests pass.
- Spec: review amendment and SCENARIO-ARC-WMTE-7046-C. Flag ledger evidence.
- Note `docs/research-notes/grammar-27b-trial-2026-09-05.md` is complete
  and tracked: proof tables, both fix rounds, the trial, and its limits.
- Harness `scripts/experiments/outer_loop_arc_grammar_27b_trial_20260905.py`:
  one card via CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, placement read from nvidia-smi joined
  on UUID, non-default port, receipt armed, server killed by exact PID,
  engine stores under the output directory, never results/**.

The 27B trial (GPU 1, 18.5 min, 14 cells) ran on the round-1 grammar
before the review landed. It shows the transport carries code on the
pinned 27B (28/28 envelopes parsed, 13 submissions, sb26 0.919 visible /
1.0 held-out at 422 tokens) and does not show unprompted submission. No
GPU time was spent after the review; nothing ran on the round-2 grammar.

Open decision: keep `list_transitions` in grammar mode with the force-turn
closure, or remove it so no argument-less envelope exists at all.

